---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_ii2_197",
  "series": "Band II 2 (1686 - 1694)",
  "seq": 197,
  "text": "<p> [[645.1]] <b>199. LEIBNIZ AN GERHARD MEIER (BREMEN)</p>\n<p> [[645.2]] Hannover, 31. Dezember 1692 (10. Januar 1693). [190.220.]</b></p>\n<p> [[645.10]] [ ... ] De prophetia perplacet quod assentiris non posse eam quae ad specialia descendit,\n[[645.11]] nisi a perfectissima mente proficisci aut in aliam mentem imprimi, itaque omnis fatidica vis a\n[[645.12]] Deo est; et oracula vera rerum singularium a daemone malo proficisci non possunt, De\n[[645.13]] Apocalypseos vera interpretatione nondum habeo, quod dicam. Interim non improbabilis mihi\n[[645.14]] visa est Grotii sententia, praedictiones ejus dirigi in Romam Ethnicam. Tantum modo numerum\n[[645.15]] bestiae quem ille quaerit in voce <greek><i>OYLPIOS</i></greek> quasi in Trajano optime principe expressum, ego\n[[645.16]] cum veteribus malim quaerere in voce <greek><i>LATEINOS</i></greek> quae et ipsa hominis denominatio est. Grotii\n[[645.17]] interpretationem, sed interpolatam renovavit nuper Episcopus Meldensis in libro quem Jurio\n[[645.18]] opposuit. Vir quidam pereruditus et ingeniosus nuper casum Hierosolymorum et poenas a\n[[645.19]] judaica gente persecutrice piorum expetitas, in Apocalypsi visus est invenisse. Interea non\n[[645.20]] ausim me illis opponere, qui in eodem vaticinio etiam totius Ecclesiae statum futurum praefiguratum\n[[645.21]] arbitrantur. Et omnino de vaticiniis sentio esse tum demum intelligenda, cum fidem\n[[645.22]] faciet dies. </p>\n<p> [[645.23]] Minutiora autem, velut Caedem Regis Angliae Caroli I., obsidionem Bremae aliaque id\n[[645.24]] genus, velle in Apocalypsi quaerere est otio abuti, et nugas agere. Tecumque sentio has nugas\n[[645.25]] seria ducere in mala, nam simplicium animos movent, et saepe reipublicae quietem turbant,\n[[645.26]] subtiliores autem, sed non satis lectione sacra et rerum judicio munitos in magnas de religionis\n[[645.27]] veritate dubitationes conjiciunt, ut veros prophetas ejusdem cum novis istis somniatoribus\n[[645.28]] farinae fuisse suspicentur. Ignotae mihi fuere Bodani Amstelodamensis Ministri praedictiones\n[[646.1]] irritae contra Viennam. Similis Quirini Kuhlmanni audacia fuit apud Londinenses tum agentis.\n[[646.2]] Is Epistolis editis jactabundis, et a sana mente remotissimis tamen apud aliquos fidem invenit.\n[[646.3]] Domum Austriacum persecutricem sanctorum, et Romam erroris sedem ajebat per Gallos\n[[646.4]] delendam; His autem cessantibus per Turcas etc. Et cum mox respondere videretur eventus,\n[[646.5]] pulso Lotharingiae duce ad Petronellam, et Turcis sedem imperatoris obsidentibus, mira fuit\n[[646.6]] Kulmannianorum triumphatio, donec soluta obsidione pudefacti conticescere cogerentur. </p>\n<p> [[646.7]] Quod ais nihil videri contingere, quod non praesciatur a causa aliqua, de Deo assentior; de\n[[646.8]] caeteris substantiis, sic putem; praesentiri quidem ab omnibus sed non praesciri, sensum scilicet\n[[646.9]] esse confusum. Quin imo ita judico tantam esse rerum omnium connexionem, ut nihil mutationis\n[[646.10]] contingat in una substantia, quod non sentiant caeterae omnes quantumcunque remotae\n[[646.11]] tempore vel loco; ita tamen ut ipsae non animadvertant. Sunt in mundo ut in microcosmo ex\n[[646.12]] Hippocratis sententia, <greek><i>sýmpnoia pánta</i></greek>. Sed consistunt hae conspirationes in motibus insensibilibus.\n[[646.13]] An vero existant praeter Deum aliae mentes tantae perspicacitatis ut praedelineationes\n[[646.14]] illas mirificae ac prope immensae subtilitatis distincte legere possint, dicere non ausim, et secus\n[[646.15]] esse suspicor, vel ideo quod effectui cuivis singulari infinitae causae intercurrunt, quoniam\n[[646.16]] continuum in infinitum divisibile est, imo divisum actu. Quodsi universum constaret ex Atomorum\n[[646.17]] numero certo, tunc sagacitas creaturarum ad perfectam cognitionem universi pervenire\n[[646.18]] posset. [ ... ] </p>\n",
  "number": "199.",
  "title": "LEIBNIZ AN GERHARD MEIER (BREMEN)",
  "date": "Hannover, 31. Dezember 1692 (10. Januar 1693). [190.220.]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:199. LEIBNIZ AN GERHARD MEIER (BREMEN) Hannover, 31. Dezember 1692 (10. Januar 1693). [190.220.] [ ... ] De prophetia perplacet quod assentiris non posse eam quae ad specialia descendit, nisi a perfectissima mente proficisci aut in aliam mentem imprimi, itaque omnis fatidica vis a Deo est; et oracul...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>